<p>14.4 These terms, the applicable standard subscription price accepted on our website or continued from your existing paid arrangement, and any separately agreed written quotation for extra work form the entire agreement. Your subscription covers the general assistance described in these terms, rather than a pre-selected list of tasks. Routine requests and acceptance of individual tasks do not vary these terms or remove the liability protections in section 12. We may use suitably competent subcontractors and remain responsible for their work within applicable legal limits. You consent to our transferring or novating this agreement to a purchaser of all or substantially all of our business or to a successor undertaking, provided that the new provider agrees to perform our contractual obligations, your contractual rights and data-protection safeguards are not materially reduced, and we give you written notice. You may transfer this agreement only with our prior written consent, not to be unreasonably withheld.</p>
<p>14.5 If a provision cannot lawfully be enforced, the rest continues so far as it can operate independently. Not enforcing a right once does not waive it in future. Only the contracting parties may enforce these terms under the Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 1999, without affecting any independent legal rights. The law and courts of England and Wales govern this agreement.</p>
<p>14.6 Continuing Protection Following Termination. Termination or expiry of this Agreement shall not affect any rights, obligations, claims or liabilities accrued before termination. All provisions which by their nature are intended to continue after termination shall remain effective, including provisions relating to: Outstanding subscription fees, unpaid invoices and lawful debt recovery; recoverable losses arising from Client breach; confidentiality and protection of commercially sensitive information; intellectual property, permitted document use and protection against misuse by competitors; limitations and exclusions of liability; Client indemnities and qualifying third-party claims; data protection, lawful retention and deletion of records; and disputes, applicable law and enforcement of contractual rights. These provisions shall continue for as long as necessary to give effect to their intended purpose, subject to applicable law and statutory limitation periods. Termination shall not release the Client from liability for breaches or payment obligations arising before termination.</p>
